    "abstract": "Parts figure for the aft cargo loading system, covering the drive unit installation, the roller trays, the loading panel, the restraint latches and the lining items disturbed by a tray change.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the aft compartment loading system items, including the loading panel, the tray joint hardware and the restraint latches at each position.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the aft compartment floor looking forward with the lining removed; sheet 2 shows one tray joint in detail. Item 40 is the swaged collar used at the tray joint on the original build; on aircraft with the short-pitch tray the joint is bolted and item 40 does not apply. Restraint latch quantities at item 50 vary with the container configuration and the figure gives the maximum."
    },
