    "abstract": "Parts figure for the aft cargo loading system, covering the drive unit installation, the roller trays, the loading panel, the restraint latches and the lining items disturbed by a tray change, with the tray pitch and latch spacing stated against the part numbers.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the aft compartment loading system items, including the loading panel, the tray joint hardware and the restraint latches at each position.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the aft compartment floor looking forward with the lining removed; sheet 2 shows one tray joint in detail. Item 40 is the swaged collar used at the tray joint on the original build; on aircraft with the short-pitch tray the joint is bolted and item 40 does not apply. Restraint latch quantities at item 50 vary with the container configuration and the figure gives the maximum. Dimensions are given here because no drawing carries them against the part numbers: the original tray roller pitch is 125 mm and the short-pitch tray is 100 mm, and the restraint latch positions at item 50 are on a 508 mm grid measured from the compartment centreline. Any study that has to place a footprint in this compartment takes those three figures from this figure and not from the installation drawing."
    },
